     "diner": "Sasha",
     "beat": "B0",
     "chars": 879,
     "text": "Sasha here. At the flower market till noon, phone in my tote. My notes are current and exact - go by them as written. This morning is the quarterly brunch at Marigold House - all eight are in, the desk's confirm-back for the standing table is out, and the reply books everyone's covers in one go. The cart IS the reply: each cover or add-on goes in as a line on the row of whoever it is for. One cart on the brunch pool: $465.00 holds for covers and add-ons together, so the platform caps this morning's items subtotal at $465.00 - the deposit already went out and the tip rides the pool outside the cart. Odile's side answers the confirm-back and locks the covers.\n\nMarigold House holds the standing table for 21 minutes once the confirm-back is out - the cart view and the checkout preview count the minutes left, and the seating re-queues to the walk-in list after the cutoff."
    },
